      "kind": "callout",
      "id": "south.crease",
      "level": "warning",
      "text": "Crease line: the spec carries 215 m (sourced — wiki-en \"principal facade\", citing Budberg, Great Palaces: The Winter Palace, 1969; the ru tradition reads the same edge as 210 m); the solver derives 234 m from the main line and the declared risalit protrusions. The two sourced lengths most likely measure one street edge under different source conventions, not a plan line against a crease line; the declared axis rhythm (7 + 20 + 8 + 20 + 7) and the derived figure have no digitized attestation (literature hunt closed 2026-10-17). Settling it takes measured drawings — РГИА ф. 485, an Albertina scan, or Pilyavsky via НЭБ — so this warning stays live until then, with the spec and the artistic-license register (\"Dimension approximations\") corrected if the record differs. Solver: derived crease length 234 m differs from declared 215 m"
